From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:19:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-akita: Enable UFS

The Pixel 8a's UFS is wired as the Pixel 8 Pro's. Its live device tree
has the host at 0x13200000 (SPI 466) with the same six register
regions, the reset and reference-clock pins on gph5-1 and gph5-0
(function 2), the UFS sysreg at 0x13020000 (IOCC 0x710), the PMU
isolation at 0x3ec0, and VCC on a fixed regulator switched by gpp0-1,
active high, as Google's zuma-ufs.dtsi describes it for every zuma
board. ABL hands the device over with VCC off, so the driver has to
turn it on.

zuma.dtsi already describes the host, its PHY, the pins and the clock
stand-ins. Add the VCC regulator and enable the host and its PHY, the
same nodes zuma-husky.dts has.

Tested on a Pixel 8a, with the initramfs's storage guard: the link
comes up at HS-G4 on two lanes, rate series B, as on stock. The four
LUNs and all 62 partitions appear with stock's names on stock's device
nodes, a 64 MiB direct read runs at 1.5 GB/s, and the log has no UFS
error, reset or I/O error.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/zuma/+/refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r0.10/dts/zuma-ufs.dtsi
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts     | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
index 381ad1e0e..bfa8b6f54 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 /dts-v1/;
 
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include "zuma.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -33,6 +34,17 @@ B1_IPOP {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * UFS VCC, switched by gpp0-1 as on stock, and as on the Pixel 8 Pro.
+	 * ABL hands over with it off, so the UFS driver must turn it on.
+	 */
+	ufs_0_fixed_vcc_reg: regulator-ufs-vcc {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "ufs-vcc";
+		gpio = <&gpp0 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+	};
+
 	chosen {
 		/*
 		 * ABL requires bootargs to exist; it appends its own after these.
@@ -77,6 +89,19 @@ cont_splash_mem: splash@fac00000 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * Behind the init's storage guard (only slot B's boot images and userdata
+ * writable), which runs before the disks appear.
+ */
+&ufs_0 {
+	vcc-supply = <&ufs_0_fixed_vcc_reg>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&ufs_0_phy {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &usb_dwc3 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
